---
description: Active engine and client/server authority boundary
alwaysApply: true
---

- The active root game is **React + Framer Motion + TypeScript**. `pnpm dev` does not run
  Phaser. Do not invent imports from nonexistent `client/src/game/` paths.
- Phaser code in `experiments/loot-drop/` is archived reference material, excluded from the
  root app. Do not treat it as production or copy stale socket contracts from it.
- The server (`server/src/engine.ts`) is authoritative. React renders public/private state and
  sends intents; it never computes correct answers, random outcomes or score mutations.
- Shared pure logic belongs in `shared/src/game/`; named values belong in `shared/src/config/`;
  socket/state types belong in `shared/src/types/index.ts`.
- Animation timelines must tolerate late/out-of-order state, cancel on phase/question changes
  and reconstruct from current state after reconnect.
- A future renderer migration requires an explicit architecture decision and preservation of
  the complete two-device multiplayer loop. Do not start one as incidental visual cleanup.
- Canonical architecture: `docs/context/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
